index 00000000..e1c95f34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/mobile/phase2a-local-ios-status.md
@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
+# Phase 2A local iOS repository foundation status
+
+## Verdict
+
+`VALIDATED ON IOS SIMULATOR`
+
+This status applies only to Phase 2A local-only behavior on the validated iOS simulator.
+
+It is not a release-readiness or cross-platform claim.
+
+## Security boundary
+
+The owned iOS method channel stores only the Ed25519 seed and account session token in Keychain.
+
+Both use `kSecAttrAccessibleAfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly`.
+
+This accessibility supports the intended post-unlock local background needs while preventing migration to a different device through backup restore.
+
+The Keychain queries set `kSecAttrSynchronizable` to false, so neither secret uses iCloud Keychain synchronization.
+
+The Keychain service and account names are fixed and bounded in the Swift boundary.
+
+No secret bytes, bearer tokens, authorization headers, or private keys are emitted in application logs or diagnostic UI.
+
+The Dart boundary reports typed unavailable, locked, malformed, and OS-status failures.
+
+Duplicate Keychain writes are resolved with the explicit update path rather than being treated as a successful new insert.
+
+Android returns the typed `platformUnsupported` failure from the secure-store boundary.
+
+No Android fallback to SharedPreferences was added.
+
+## Migration and identity behavior
+
+The legacy `identity/ed25519Seed` value is copied to Keychain only after 32-byte validation.
+
+The write is read back byte-for-byte before the legacy preference is removed.
+
+Conflicting valid legacy and Keychain seeds fail closed without rotation or deletion.
+
+The schema-defined opaque `nodeId` is stored separately from the Ed25519 public key.
+
+The legacy `auth/session` JSON retains non-secret metadata only after its non-empty session token has been written to and verified from Keychain.
+
+Session loading combines that metadata with the Keychain token in memory.
+
+Logout removes the session token and retains the node seed.
+
+## Local repository behavior
+
+Canonical repositories live at `<Application Support>/ForkMesh/repositories/<repoId>/worktree`.
+
+They are never created in Documents or shared storage.
+
+The app uses the iOS sandbox's default restrictive directory permissions.
+
+Canonical repositories are persistent user state rather than disposable caches, so Phase 2A does not exclude them from backup.
+
+Phase 2A creates no disposable repository cache that requires a backup-exclusion attribute.
+
+All generated path components are validated, and malformed identifiers, separators, traversal, NUL bytes, symlink targets, and non-directory repository roots fail closed.
+
+Each app-created repository has a cryptographically random canonical 128-bit `fmrepo_` ID.
+
+Its exact immutable `.forkmesh/repository.json` manifest is written atomically, validated by read-back, and committed as the bootstrap commit.
+
+One app-private replica metadata record binds the repository ID, local node ID, and sandbox location.
+
+Replica metadata is written atomically and records the local canonical head.
+
+Create and explicit local-replica removal use an operation journal that is recovered before the repository boundary is exposed.
+
+Removing a local replica requires an explicit `removeLocalReplica` intent and has no remote or catalog effect.
+
+## Capability boundary
+
+Enabled local capabilities are `git.localRepository`, `git.localAuthoring`, `git.offlineBrowse`, `git.localBranch`, and `git.localCommit`.
+
+`git.clone`, `git.fetch`, `git.push`, and `git.untrustedSha1Import` are disabled with `awaitingIndependentCryptographyReview`.
+
+`git.remoteHosting` is disabled with `phaseNotImplemented`.
+
+`git.androidRuntime` is disabled with `androidSdkUnavailable`.
+
+The physical-device validation blocker remains `physicalDeviceValidationPending`.
+
+The production adapter returns typed errors for every disabled operation below the UI boundary.
+
+It uses only the local ForkMesh-owned `forkmesh_git` package and has no process or system-Git fallback.
+
+## Validation evidence
+
+The focused Flutter tests cover seed and session migration, restart, failed secure writes, conflicting seeds, repository creation and reopening, local text and binary authoring, branch checkout, path safety, crash recovery, and typed remote denial.
+
+The iOS simulator `EA3FD115-8BD0-478B-8340-F273CCB0BAEE` passed the Keychain/Application Support probe and the full Phase 2A local repository probe on 2026-07-16.
+
+The local probe migrated real simulator Keychain state, restarted identity, created and reopened an app-sandbox repository, committed text and binary files, created and checked out an offline branch, read history and blobs, and verified every remote or untrusted operation is denied.
+
+The simulator build completed without changing the production iOS deployment target, which remains iOS 13.0.
+
+## Explicit remaining blockers
+
+G4.5 remains `AWAITING INDEPENDENT REVIEW`.
+
+This Phase 2A work does not approve SHA-1 collision screening, clone, fetch, push, import, hosting, G5, G6, or G7.
+
+Android is `NOT VALIDATED - SDK unavailable`.
+
+No physical iPhone runtime validation has been performed.
+
+The overall mobile phase remains `PARTIAL` until Android validation and an independent cryptography/security review are complete.
diff --git a/flutter_app/integration_test/phase2a_ios_keychain_probe_test.dart b/flutter_app/integration_test/phase2a_ios_keychain_probe_test.dart
